WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.150
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:06.425
First: payroll web's web dot
config uses integrated security.

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:08.512
Why does the scan put it in column A?

4
00:00:08.512 --> 00:00:13.800
The answer is b: it runs on an Arc host
with Microsoft Data SQL Client five point

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.352
two point two, at or above
the managed identity release,

6
00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:19.799
so the move is a configuration change.

7
00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:24.275
Second: which three conditions must hold
before a connection string changes?

8
00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:28.188
The answer is a: the Entra login
exists, it holds the database role,

9
00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:32.175
and the change is tested in a
production-equivalent environment.

10
00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:36.530
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.
